      "writtenOn": "2025-03-04T18:08:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One thing that I just thought about is if the hash would be stable over time or is it possible the hash function changes (or different Java implementations could implement different hash functions), so then the link that brought you to a particular string may not work across all ahat instances. It would be nice if we could guarantee that the ID used for the string is stable across time so that a particular link will always work correctly. Perhaps it could be a standardized hash, like SHA256 (or maybe something more lightweight).",
      "revId": "97e0d576772116e543bc684fb3f1f975f345d09b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fbdf73de_b238ea60",
        "filename": "tools/ahat/src/main/com/android/ahat/ObjectsHandler.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 2058033
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-05T12:26:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I suppose I could do something like `SHA256` but I don\u0027t think it is necessary to change it.\n\nIIUC, because we use `.hashCode()` here and `.hashCode()` in the summarizer which provides the link, the hashing algorithm will always be the same as we are running it in the same execution ([doc](https://docs.oracle.com/javase/7/docs/api/java/lang/Object.html#hashCode()) ) so will always return the same value, regardless of if the algorithm itself changes.",
      "parentUuid": "1fd559b6_998a3589",
      "revId": "97e0d576772116e543bc684fb3f1f975f345d09b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e08fb1bd_e434f529",
        "filename": "tools/ahat/src/main/com/android/ahat/ObjectsHandler.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 1565050
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-05T12:33:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What I\u0027m referring to is if you give someone a link, like http://localhost:7100/objects?class\u003djava.lang.String\u0026stringHash\u003d325967270\n\nToday, for all the links that you can send, the receiver of the link should be able to run their own copy of ahat with the same hprof file and see exactly what you see when you follow that link. If they run with a different Java implementation, then the link may send them to a different string (or there may be no matching string at all).",
      "parentUuid": "fbdf73de_b238ea60",
      "revId": "97e0d576772116e543bc684fb3f1f975f345d09b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
